  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $l=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{[\\sin x]}{x} ; \\mathrm{RHL}=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0^{+}} \\frac{\\sin x}{x}=1$<br />$\\mathrm{LHL}=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0^{-}}\\left(\\frac{-\\sin x}{x}\\right)=-\\left(\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0^{-}} \\frac{\\sin x}{x}\\right)=-1$<br />$\\left[|x|=\\begin{array}{c}x \\text { if } x \\geq 0 \\\\ -x \\text { if } x \\leq 0\\end{array}\\right]$<br />As, LHL $\\neq$ RHL Hence, limit $l$.does not exist.",
    "image": null
  },
